# Units masked on every enrolled host, one per line, with the reason.
#
# This file is the source of truth: scripts/deploy.sh masks everything listed
# here, on every host in FLEET. It does NOT unmask anything, so removing a line
# is not enough to undo it - see CLAUDE.md.
#
# Only put a unit here if it should be masked on the WHOLE fleet. A unit that is
# noise on one host is a per-host decision and does not belong in a file that
# claims to describe all fourteen.

# Ships as a dependency of ipmitool. The unit is an LSB init script that loads
# the in-band IPMI driver, and there is no /dev/ipmi* on any host - lenora
# included, so the BMC on that board is not exposed in-band either. It was the
# fleet's only failed unit, which made the systemd-unit-failed alert in
# grafana/ useless: it had to exclude the one thing that was actually failing.
# For in-band ipmitool on lenora, unmask and load ipmi_si/ipmi_devintf;
# out-of-band over LAN never needed this.
openipmi.service
